@startuml monitor_record_model
' Spectracs — the MonitorRecord object model: what a monitored acquisition produces,
' where each piece lives, and which of them reach the PDF.
' Companion to spectracsPy/docs/SPEC_settled_measurement.md §15.2 / §18 / §27.12 / §27.13.
' Regenerate:  java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg monitor_record_model.puml

title Spectracs — MonitorRecord & the settling views\nwhat a monitored run produces, and where it lives (as-built 2026-08-17)

hide circle
hide empty methods
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor<<runtime>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<runtime>> #666666
  BackgroundColor<<persisted>> #CDE7CE
  BorderColor<<persisted>> #2E7D32
  BackgroundColor<<sdk>> #FFE6CC
  BorderColor<<sdk>> #B36A00
  BackgroundColor<<view>> #EAF2FB
  BorderColor<<view>> #3A6EA5
  BackgroundColor<<enum>> #FFF7E6
  BorderColor<<enum>> #B58900
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B36A00
  BackgroundColor #FFF7E6
}

legend right
  |= colour |= tier |
  | <#FFE6CC>  | plugin_sdk (Qt-free, spectracsPy-core) |
  | <#FFFFFF>  | runtime only — dies with the run |
  | <#CDE7CE>  | persisted (app DB) |
  | <#EAF2FB>  | view-model (renders to Qt AND to paper) |
endlegend

' ===================== the run's product =====================

class MonitorResult <<sdk>> {
  + outcome : MonitorOutcome
  + rows : [MonitorRow]          'ALL rows, ~1700 for 20 min
  + spectrum                     '⭐ the ANSWER's window mean
  + answer : {valueKey, value, t,\n   frameIndex, readAs, branch}
  + columns : [{key,label,unit}] '⭐ self-describing
  + policy : MonitorPolicy
  + evaluatorId / evaluatorVersion
  + clearingSeconds              '⭐ a sigma_fill component
  + cancelled / capsHit / error
  + distinctFraction             '§23/V1 duplicate-frame budget
  + notes : [str]
  + views : [ReportableView]     '⭐ §27.12 — the SAME objects on the step
  --
  + hasValue()
  + decisionRows()               '⭐ only THESE persist (~35)
  + toRecord() : MonitorRecord
}

class MonitorRow <<sdk>> {
  + t          '⚠ window CENTRE, not "when the line was written"
  + frameIndex 'global index of the window's LAST frame
  + n / nAccepted
  + values : {}  '⚠ the PLUGIN's scalars — MAY BE EMPTY
  + provisional / isDecisionRow
  --
  + toDict()   'flattens `values` into the row
}

class MonitorPolicy <<sdk>> {
  + windowFrames / retentionFrames
  + minWindowFrames
  + evaluateEveryNFrames
  + maxSeconds   '⛔ NEVER None — §12.2 termination
  + maxFrames
}

enum MonitorOutcome <<enum>> {
  SETTLED_IMMEDIATE
  SETTLED_AFTER_CLEARING
  COMPLETED
  --
  NEVER_SETTLED
  MEASUREMENT_BROKEN
  CANCELLED
  STALLED
  FAILED
}

MonitorResult "1" *-- "0..*" MonitorRow
MonitorResult --> MonitorPolicy
MonitorResult --> MonitorOutcome

note bottom of MonitorRow
  ⛔ NOTHING in the engine may index into `values`.
  The host knows `t` and `answer["valueKey"]` —
  never what `Q%` means (§15.2).
end note

' ===================== the travelling record =====================

class "MonitorRecord\n(a plain dict — JSON only)" as REC <<persisted>> {
  outcome / cancelled / capsHit
  evaluatorId / evaluatorVersion
  policy : {}      'two runs under different rules
  clearingSeconds  '  must never be compared silently
  distinctFraction
  columns : []
  answer : {}
  rows : []        '⚠ a LIST with `t` as a VALUE —
  notes : []       '  never a map keyed by a float
}

MonitorResult ..> REC : toRecord()

class SpectralWorkflow <<persisted>> {
  + monitorRecordJson : Text
  + sectionedPhasesJson : Text   '⭐ D4 — which phases
  --                             '  are sectioned by STEP
  + getMonitorRecord() / setMonitorRecord()
  + getSectionedPhases() / setSectionedPhases()
  + toReportJson() -> {..., "monitorRecord",\n                    "sectionedPhases"}
}

note right of SpectralWorkflow #E3F2FD
  ⭐⭐ D4 (§27.14a) — THE STRUCTURE IS PART OF THE
  RECORD. The plugin declares it once (stamped at
  run start from NavigationPolicy.stepChevronPhases);
  the chevron, the PDF's section headings and a
  plugin-free LIMS addon all read it from HERE.
  ⛔ Before this it lived only in the live host, so a
  re-opened run showed one "Acquisition" chevron
  where the measurement showed Reference > Sample.
  ⚠ Only the STRUCTURE persists — `mode`
  (STEP/AUTO_ADVANCE) is interaction, not a fact
  about the measurement.
end note

class "PDF /EmbeddedFiles\n  workflow.json" as PDFJSON <<runtime>>

REC --> SpectralWorkflow : stored whole, for EVERY outcome\n⭐ incl. the runs with no value
SpectralWorkflow ..> PDFJSON : the MACHINE half of the report

' ===================== the human half =====================

class SpectralWorkflowStep <<persisted>> {
  + role  'SAMPLE
  + _view '⚠ TRANSIENT (@reconstructor) — see note
  + container
  + evaluationResult
}

class EvaluationResult <<persisted>> {
  + resultJson : Text
  + items : [ReportableView]
}

class TabGroupView <<view>> {
  + tabs : [(label, view | [view])]
  + isShownInReport = True
  + isMonitorView  '✅ round-trips (D2)
}

class "Overview\nLabelView + 11x MetricFieldView" as OV <<view>>
class "Q% · Turbidity · Rate\n3x SeriesPlotView" as CURVES <<view>>
class "Health · Decisions\n2x TableView" as TABLES <<view>>

SpectralWorkflowStep *-- EvaluationResult
EvaluationResult *-- TabGroupView
TabGroupView *-- OV
TabGroupView *-- CURVES
TabGroupView *-- TABLES
MonitorResult --> TabGroupView : views[0] is the SAME object\n⭐ ONE construction, ONE home

note right of TabGroupView #C8E6C9
  ✅ §27.13b / D1 — FIXED 2026-08-17
  The curve and table tabs carry
  isShownInReport = False and are now
  HONOURED: willDrawInReport() filters
  the children, so paper gets the
  Overview alone (3 pages -> 1, measured)
  while the SCREEN still shows all six —
  the GUI ignores the flag by contract.
end note

note right of SpectralWorkflowStep #E3F2FD
  ⭐ WHY THE TABS ARE INVISIBLE LIVE AND
  VISIBLE WHEN RE-OPENED (§27.12 / §27.13d):
  renderStep() routes a step whose _view is a
  CaptureView to the capture panel, which never
  reads the EvaluationResult. `_view` is
  @reconstructor-transient ⇒ a step loaded from
  the DB has none, falls through to the passive
  visitor, and the tabs come back.
  ✅ No longer an accident: pinned by
  test_saved_run_shows_the_settling_tabs.py and
  argued in renderStep()'s own comment, because
  "persist the view descriptor" would otherwise
  delete the tabs from every re-opened run.
end note

note bottom of EvaluationResult #C8E6C9
  ✅ §27.13c / D2 — FIXED 2026-08-17. The tag has a
  class default on ReportableView and is written and
  read by TabGroupView, so it survives the real DB ⇒
  a re-measure inside a reloaded run REPLACES.
end note

@enduml
